### MMLongBench-Doc row 0434

The answer identifies **Kaggle’s Cat vs Dog dataset** and connects it to the “coding time” section. The actual final-generation request user message is 1,337 characters (SHA-256 `dc34b4a5b81d7578679603f978e262d67d27262cab9ab5f24acb354129ae7669`). It contains the actual “Coding time!” evidence and the next source chunk’s exact sentence: **“Kaggle's Cat vs Dog dataset (25k dog/cat pictures)”**. Thus the 25k detail was delivered to the final model input and appears in the answer.

The answer cites chunk IDs `084c5bee-f7be-4718-9c0b-510e61cb401a` and `10ff171b-a054-4cbc-9ab4-4c52b8c3022f`. Both saved readbacks returned HTTP 200 in the same KB and resolved to current document/version identities. The answer’s `doc` attribute is a filename-stem display alias; the chunk IDs and KB ID match the readback records.

Observed path counts: 30 retrieval candidates → 1 rerank → 1 merge → 4 projected sources → 4 context evidence items. These counts do not establish any particular strategy rule activation.

### LongBench-ZH DuReader

The answer is a Chinese, structured response on task refresh and task-loop methods. The final model input contains 11 selected evidence items, including native text on the water/equipment task loop, time rollback with a new shelter and task refresh, and save/reload steps that change box-opening RNG. The source also supports the house expansion/no-upgrade advice. I therefore assess the core instructions as substantially source-supported.

The frozen local Gold sidecar says the official answer string was not located. This is a manual semantic comparison with frozen native reference answers, **not an official benchmark accuracy result**. The answer has no citation tags, and its exported `sources.json` is empty; this is a citation failure even though the evidence was present in the generation context. “Most common,” “most general and efficient,” and “non-destructive” are not established by the delivered sources as phrased. The answer is well structured but overlong and mixes the main farming mechanics with extra advice and caveats.

Observed path counts: 30 retrieval candidates → 11 rerank → 3 merge → 11 projected sources → 11 context evidence items. No answer-correctness or strategy activation is inferred from those counts.

### HotpotQA

The answer names **Pieter van Musschenbroek** as the person credited with both inventions. It cites the Leyden-jar and tribometer facts. Saved HTTP 200 readbacks resolve the cited chunk IDs to current documents/versions in the scoped KB; the additional jar-definition citation also resolves. The final generation context contains both supporting passages.

Observed path counts: 30 retrieval candidates → 8 rerank → 8 merge → 5 projected sources → 5 context evidence items.

## Evidence and limits

Per-case raw answer SHA-256, actual final request path/hash, request ID, final user-message hash/length, compact stage counts, and evidence-file hashes are recorded in the adjacent JSON. Source readbacks and selected final-context evidence were reviewed; this is an offline agent quality review, not an Owner sign-off.

The reported runtime figure of 16 settled calls / 40,977 tokens is an execution-accounting total, not a quality score. No strategy-rule activation is claimed based only on the returned answer or stage counts.
